problem:
The lattice shown is continued for $9$ rows. What will be the third number in the $9$th row? \begin{tabular}{rccccc}
Row 1: & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 \\
Row 2: & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 & 10 \\
Row 3: & 11 & 12 & 13 & 14 & 15 \\
Row 4: & 16 & 17 & 18 & 19 & 20
\end{tabular}

solution:
Recall that multiplication and division should be done before addition and subtraction. We get  \begin{align*}
4+10\div2-2\cdot3&=4+5-6\\
&=9-6\\
&=\boxed{3}.
\end{align*}

There are 18 total slices, and 10 of them have pepperoni and 10 have mushrooms. Let there be $n$ slices that have both.  Then there are $10-n$ with only pepperoni and $10-n$ with mushrooms.  The total number of slices then is $n+(10-n)+(10-n)=18$.  Simplifying gives $20-n = 18$, so $n=\boxed{2}$:


